      "message": "Hi. I was able to observe a similar situation while running the `timer` test on `bloonchipper` with `stress -c $(nproc)` running in the background. The `run_device_test.py` script would report a timeout due to lack of the `Pass!`. To check if the message is send by Renode I\u0027ve dumped the UART output to an additional file and in that file the message was visible (see: https://renode.readthedocs.io/en/latest/host-integration/uart.html#redirecting-to-a-file on what to add to the `.resc` script to do that). This may suggest that with high loads on the host machine some messages from Renode are dropped. For me this was reproducible only with with `stress` running on all available cores.",
